  "context": "# Goal\nTameshi round 37, verification-fixture craft. This is a v1 falsification wave for the frozen claims in /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin/.ufo/evidence/round-37/contract.json and the artifacts it names. C1 tests the r36 control-input resolvability repair; C2 tests bounded ANSI-C `$'...'` comment handling in `tools/tally-audit-v3.py`, not a full shell lexer. The L1 holds the canonical planner seat; do not add a planner role.\n\n# Dispatch dependency\nThis prepared w2 is eligible only after a dispatched w1 returns at least 32 distinct concrete attack items. If that condition is not demonstrated, do not dispatch w2. These specs are prepared artifacts only until the orchestrator elects to dispatch them.\n\n# Hard write and process bounds\nLane repo: /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin. Every `Report:` trailer is relative to that lane root: write it at /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin/<that path>. Each writer must use its own actual worktree, unique branch/path, and observed base; no concurrent writers on the live checkout. Seats are leaves, never spawn. Never mutate the lane Git index, jj state, `.git`, `.ufo/state`, fleet repo, sibling lane, or source tree. Write only the assigned report under `.ufo/waves/round-37/w2/`; findings are read-only.\n\n# Routing and tooling\nUse the role-to-route table in /home/vgpnk/.omp/agent/config.yml; never pass a model. Operator tooling authorization permits helpful official-source tools, but pacman transactions are PAUSED host-wide: do not run pacman; use uv/npx/official binary if needed and record any install/version/channel/reason. No install is required unless evidence proves otherwise.\n\n# Frozen boundaries\nDo not change claim predicates, post-data counter logic, source IDs, or tool pins. The committed empty-panel manifest binds the source panel tree `4f3d8af5b62ba04a5ff825bfdaec6c9193f8489e`; the C2 code-view predicate is exactly the two ANSI-C fixtures. Report every false pass, false fail, setup failure, or scope overclaim with full observed output.",
